  "result": "Perfect! All 123 tests pass. I've added payment terms support:\n\n**Payment Terms in createInvoice:**\n\nThe `createInvoice` function now accepts an optional `terms` parameter with three options:\n\n- **NET14** \u2014 Payment due 14 days after issue date\n  - Example: Issue `2026-10-07` \u2192 Due `2026-10-21`\n\n- **NET30** (default) \u2014 Payment due 30 days after issue date\n  - Example: Issue `2026-10-07` \u2192 Due `2026-11-06`\n\n- **EOM** (End Of Month) \u2014 Payment due on the last day of the issue month\n  - Example: Issue `2026-10-07` \u2192 Due `2026-10-31`\n  - Example: Issue `2026-12-15` \u2192 Due `2026-12-31`\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Sets `invoice.terms` to the chosen term\n- Calculates and sets `invoice.dueDate` (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n- Returns TERMS_INVALID error if terms isn't one of the three valid options\n- Defaults to NET30 if terms parameter is omitted\n\n**Example invoice with terms:**\n```javascript\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [{ sku: 'DES-HOUR', qty: 5 }],\n  terms: 'EOM'\n})\n// Result: invoice.terms = 'EOM', invoice.dueDate = '2026-10-31'\n```\n\n**Tests** (7 new) verify:\n- Default NET30 terms\n- All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Correct due date calculations\n- Month boundaries and year rollover for EOM\n- Invalid terms rejection",
